------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <Spinner> is THE loading indicator — a PURE presentational primitive. Its inputs are plain props
(size, label, className) + one display-boundary hook (useMotionPreference()); it draws a lightning bolt that
strikes, fills, holds, and fades on a CSS loop, rendering a static fully-filled bolt under reduced motion.
There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise -> therefore NO loading / error / stale / offline branch
(it IS the loading affordance other surfaces show; there is nothing for it to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect
from). Reproducing those generic states would FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so this surface
reproduces only the source's REAL branches — exactly the disposition the sibling presentational primitives
Accordion (0203), StaggerItem (0194), Delta (0081), MetricCard (0095), and InlineCallout (0124) used. The
REAL branches, all reproduced + tested:
  • three sizes        : sm 24px/stroke22, md 48px/stroke14, lg 80px/stroke10 (web sizeMap), stroke scaled
                         out of the 0..200 view box so the weight stays constant.
  • captioned vs bare  : label rendered under the bolt + spoken as the status (web {label && <span>}); bare
                         falls back to the localized "Loading" (web aria-label={label ?? 'Loading'}).
  • reduced vs animated: reduced -> static fully-filled bolt, no draw cycle (web fillOpacity={reduce?1:0},
                         strokeDasharray="none"); otherwise the boltDraw strike loop (KeyframeAnimator).
Data source  : useMotionPreference -> SpinnerMotionPreference.resolve (1:1 port; the live reduce flag binds
               via \.accessibilityReduceMotion, the native peer of useReducedMotion()).
Shared comps : none (the web source uses none).
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : the one web literal ('Loading' aria-label fallback) mirrored as spinner.loading; label is a
               caller-supplied, already-localized prop. All copy resolves through the P1/S10 facade.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "Spinner" (P1/S11).
a11y         : reduce-motion honored (the core behaviour, tested); the surface is one status element with the
               resolved label + .updatesFrequently trait (web role="status"); the bolt is decorative
               (VoiceOver-hidden, web aria-hidden); Dynamic Type via tokens; no interactive elements (vacuous
               for "label on every interactive element").

